            <ArticleTitle>Abruptio placentae.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>865-75</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Despite our heightened awareness of placental abruption, this condition remains largely unpreventable. The incidence of placental abruption may actually be on the rise due to increasing use of cocaine and &quot;crack&quot; and a greater contribution from abdominal trauma. Whether recurrence of abruption associated with hypertension can be prevented with low-dose aspirin is yet to be determined. Unfortunately, although our recognition of this condition may have improved, placental abruption remains a high cause of perinatal morbidity and mortality.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
